  "rationale": "<p>The correct answer is <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that the function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> is defined by <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals x plus eight elevenths\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"three elevenths\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></math>for <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> in the given function yields <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis three elevenths right parenthesis equals three elevenths plus eight elevenths\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></math>, which gives <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis three elevenths right parenthesis equals StartFraction 11 Over 11 EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></math>,&nbsp;or <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis three elevenths right parenthesis equals 1\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Therefore, when <math alttext=\"x equals three elevenths\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></math>, the value of <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>.</p>",
